.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-discover-device - Describe a pveforge device-semantic resolver's schema (layer 2, purely local — no target/roster needed)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge discover device [type] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Describe a pveforge device-semantic resolver's schema: the fields it takes
and what each accepts. This is layer 2 of discover, pveforge's own device
model, which PVE's schema cannot describe. It is purely local: no target,
roster or connection is needed.

.PP
With no type, it lists the types it can describe, under the key types. The
types are: NVMeDrive. A type is matched exactly, case included.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for device

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="kv"
	output format: "kv" or "json"


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-discover(1)\fP
